racy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 07 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast lesion   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fibroadipose tissue fragment with a localization needle  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal approximately 80  fibrosis with focal hemorrhage and several clear fluid containing cysts ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 0 2cm in diameter  The remaining 20  of the specimen consists of yellow fatty tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes A through I  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left lateral breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fibroadipose tissue fragment which is inked  serially sectioned and submitted into in cassettes J and K  Resident  QUN DONG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  LEFT LATERAL   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 50 CLINICAL DATA  Status post right mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LET   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL ADENOCARCINOMA  95    POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 3 3   EXTENDING TO THE RESECTION MARGINS AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  5    CRIBRIFORM TYPE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor is 0 5cm in size  There is focal perineural invasion  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 11                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 08 09     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   LEFT  BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   2   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 463 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 5  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    The analysis is suboptional because of crush artifact and scant tumor  Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 56 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Left breast  is a 4 x 3 x 2cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue with a localizing wire and accompanying x ray which shows a lesion adjacent to the wire  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm firm white focus  0 1cm from the nearest margin  No frozen is done  Tissue for BRDU and estrogen receptors are submitted to Cox 5  Section Code  A B  lesion and surrounding tissue  C L  entire remainder  Resident  Daniel D  Koelliker  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST LEFT BIOPSY   SMALL FOCUS SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA BUT TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 AUG 97 ACCESSIONED ON  26 AUG 97 at 12 46 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST   LEFT SUPERIOR BREAST  TWO LESIONS    BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  THREE NODULAR FOCI EACH MEASURES REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE AND REMOVED_DATE CM  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED SURFACES AND WITH FOCAL PERINEURAL INVASION   SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  ASSOCIATED WITH AND EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  AND TO REMOVED_DATE CM OF AN INKED MARGIN  Note  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion are not seen  All three foci  nodules  of invasive carcinoma are histologically similar and most likely represent one primary lesion  intramammary metastasis is less likely  but cannot be excluded  BREAST   LEFT BREAST MASS  INFERIOR WIRE    BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  PRESENT AT AN INKED SURFACE   SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE ASSOCIATED WITH AND EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE COMPONENT AND TO SEVERAL INKED SURFACES  Note  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The carcinoma is histologically similar to the three invasive nodules present in the first specimen  see above   and most likely represent the same primary carcinoma  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  28 AUG 97 at 16 11                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  left  All Four Masses  The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 09 17 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left superior breast  two lesions   are two pieces of tissue  The largest tissue is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm and contains a 2 2cm firm tan mass with infiltrative borders  Representative section of the mass are frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  Tumor approaches ink  Representative sections of the larger tissue are submitted in cassettes A through C  The smaller REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm specimen contains two tan yellow  firm masses 1 0cm in diameter each  with infiltrative margins  Lesion entirely submitted in cassettes D through F  Normal breast are submitted in G through H  Received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name  unit number and  left breast mass  inferior wire  is a 3 x 3 x 1cm fragment of breast tissue with localizing wire  Specimen inked and sectioned to reveal a firm  tan and focally yellow  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm mass  abutting inked margins  Mass is submitted in I K and representative section of surrounding breast in L  Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LARGE LEFT SUPERIOR BREAST MARGIN  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  LESS THAN 1MM FROM MARGIN  GROSS DIAGNOSIS    LEFT BREAST MASS  INFERIOR WIRE     SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  AWAIT PERMANENTS  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT SUPERIOR SMALLER NODULES   NODULES SUSPICIOUS INVASIVE CARCINOMA  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Suzanne B  Keel  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT  INFERIOR    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
