rected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 8cm right simple mastectomy with a short stitch designating the superior margin and a long stitch designating the lateral margin  The anterior aspect is inked blue  and the posterior is inked black  There is an overlying 4 0cm nipple areolar complex that is grossly unremarkable  Sectioning of the specimen reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm irregular firm mass in the lower outer quadrant of the specimen with a grossly visible biopsy tract within the mass  The mass measures 9 0cm from the superior aspect  3 5cm from the inferior aspect  2 0cm from the lateral aspect  and 9 2cm from the medial aspect of the mastectomy specimen  The mass abuts the anterior margin and measures 1 2cm from the closest posterior resection margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  No intraparenchymal lymph nodes are seen  The specimen is submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the mass with closest anterior resection margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the mass with closest posterior resection margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the mass with biopsy site   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections of the 6 8cm mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section from the axillary tail region  Final Diagnosis by Adriana Dionigi Corben M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  2 RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast   Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  544  to chromosome 17 signals  156  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be interpreted with caution  Addendum  2 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   Breast  Right   Simple Mastectomy  report_end  , Unchecked.
