cimen is inked black on the sutured side  and the smaller portion is inked black entirely  The larger portion is bisected and submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the smaller portion is submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final medial   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm fragment of tan pink tissue with a suture on one side indicating the margin  The sutured side is inked black entirely and the specimen is submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast additional   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm unoriented fatty portion of soft tissue  that is bivalved and frozen entirely as frozen section  1  now resubmitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION   1  SOFT TISSUE  LEFT BREAST ADDITIONAL   LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  Gross Dictation by Matthew M Johnson M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCIS