Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  UpdatedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Frozen Section Pathologist  Lawrence R Zukerberg  M D  Frozen Section Resident  Aleksandr Vasilyev  M D  Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Pavan K Auluck  M D   Ph D  Reports To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Tissue Processed Reason for Addendum  3  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  Right breast cancer  invasive ductal   FINAL DIAGNOSIS  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA  SENTINEL   EXCISION  METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  SEE TABLE  2 BELOW   BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MIXED CONVENTIONAL AND MICROPAPILLARY TYPE   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE TABLE  1  METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN 11 OF 20 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  SEE TABLE  2 BELOW   TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm  GRADE  3  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Present  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within the region of the mass  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS  2 SUMMARY OF AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  INCLUDING SENTINEL NODES  TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES  12 TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  22 Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   3 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   9  largest deposit spans 1 8cm   Extracapsular extension  None  Other forms of axillary involvement  Lymphatic vessels  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue with two potential lymph nodes  The specimen is bisected and one half is frozen as FX 1 which is now submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remaining half is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x 14 x 4 7cm modified radical mastectomy containing a skin ellipse measuring 25 x 11 5cm and a 10 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm axillary tail  The specimen is oriented with a single suture marking 12 o clock  There is also an area of green dye lateral to the nipple in the center of the skin ellipse  The anterior resection margin of the specimen is inked blue  the posterior resection margin is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to demonstrate a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm reddish gray mass located superior and posterior to the nipple  as close as 1 1cm from the superior margin  1 5cm from the posterior margin  1 7cm from the anterior margin and greater than 2cm from all other margins  A small amount of milky white fluid is expressed on sectioning beneath and medial to the nipple  The axillary tail is dissected to reveal multiple lymph nodes  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Radial section of the closest deep margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Area of red induration adjacent to the mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of breast parenchyma expressing white milky fluid   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of grossly unremarkable breast parenchyma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bivalved lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One potential lymph node  bivalved   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bivalved lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bivalved lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nipple  INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION   1  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE   POSITIVE FOR CARCINOMA  Gross Dictation by Pavan K Auluck M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Pavan K Auluck M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells  less than 10   stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells  less than 10   stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE Note  A section of the nipple was subsequently processed  and this slide shows high grade ductal carcinoma in situ involving the large lactiferous ducts  There is no evidence of Paget s disease or involvement of dermal lymphatics  Addendum  2 by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  863  to chromosome 17 signals  140  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  3 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 11 50 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  1 3CM  HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS PRESENT REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE ANTERIOR RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  1   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  ASSOCIATED WITH AND AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS  PRESENT REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE ANTERIOR AND INFERIOR RESECTION MARGINS   SEE NOTE  2   INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMAS  NOTE  1  No blood vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  NOTE  2  No stromal  blood vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL MARGIN    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  MICROCALCIFICATIONS ASSOCIATED WITH BENIGN DUCTS  INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMAS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 45                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     ADDENDUM  Immunohistochemical stains on formalin fixed paraffin embedded tissue shows the tumor cells are strongly positive for neuron specific enolase  faintly positive for synoptophysin  and negative for chromogranin  These findings are suggestive of carcinoma with neuroendocrine features  Added by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 30     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 09 14 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  left breast  is an unoriented breast biopsy measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  The superior margin is inked black  the inferior is inked blue  and the anterior surface is overinked green  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a 1 0cm white firm  stellate area in the lateral half of the specimen  coming within 0 4cm from the closest resection margin  superior   Representative section of the stellate area is frozen as FX 1 and is resubmitted in cassette A  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes B J  Tumor is in B F  Lateral half in G and H  and medial half in I and J  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast additional margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm irregular portion of breast tissue with a suture on one aspect marking the edge farthest from the tumor  The sutured half is black  the opposite blue  Specimen is serially sectioned to reveal no discrete lesions  Specimen is entirely submitted in K S  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  IVANA DELALLE  MD  PHD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  DR  GADD SAW THE SPECIMEN IN THE FROZEN SECTION LAB  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  ESTHER OLIVA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST LEFT  EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL MARGIN   EXCISIONAL BIOPS   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Surg General  WAC 460 MEEI MRN  REMOVED_DATE Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  CHARLES M FERGUSON  M D  Resident  Olga Kolman  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 91 year old woman with a palpable lump in the left breast at 2 00 o clock  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE SEE NOTE  NOTE  Sections of the core biopsy reveal an invasive carcinoma spanning a distance of at least 0 8cm  The tumor grows in large nests and trabeculae of malignant epithelial cells with a prominent dense lymphoid infiltrate present  The tumor cells are large and markedly pleomorphic with ill defined cytoplasm and have enlarged hyperchromatic nuclei with vesicular chromatin and prominent nucleoli  The morphologic findings are compatible with high grade invasive ductal carcinoma  The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and Her2 neu protein expression and of fluorescence in situ hybridization studies for Her2 neu gene amplification will be reported in an addendum  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast  are 6 cylindrical gray white to yellow fibrofatty soft tissue cores ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  The specimen is submitted in toto as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on Thursday REMOVED_MONTH 19   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 03 27 59PM By his her signature above  the pathologist list