Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 03 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY     LOBULAR CARCINOMA  INVASIVE   SEE NOTE      LOBULAR NEOPLASIA INCLUDING LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU AND ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  The invasive component extends to inked margins  The carcinoma measures at leasT 1 4cm in greatest dimension  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is noted  Focal microcalcifications are present  but are not in area of tumor  Immunohistochemical stain for estrogen and progesterone receptors are being performed and will be reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 18 26                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 07 23 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number   Breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm cauterized fibroadipose tissue with a localizing guide wire and an accompanying mammogram  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 0cm firm  slightly gritty  irregular tan white region focally abutting the inked resection margin  The specimen is entirely submitted in A M  with the firm region in A D and other suspicious areas from microcalcifications in F I  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT MASS   EXCISION  SUSPICIOUS AREA IS TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
