a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 AUG 95 at 15 14 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm fibroadipose tissue with wire in place and x ray demonstrating an ill defined stellate lesion  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 5cm firm gritty region with a central hemorrhagic cavity  This area is frozen as frozen section  1  and submitted in cassette A  Remaining tissue from that region is submitted in cassette B  Additional representative sections of tissue are submitted in cassettes C through O  Labeled  Axillary contents  is a piece of fibroadipose tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  Several lymph nodes are identified within this tissue  The largest lymph node is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  The largest two are bisected and submitted entirely in cassettes P and Q  respectively  Remaining lymph nodes in R through T  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   PARTIAL MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH