e the presence of myoepithelial cells around the foci of in situ and not the invasive carcinoma  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL DEEP MEDIAL INFERIOR MARGINS   EXCISION  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  An e cadherin stain does not support the presence of lobular neoplasia  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN  LATERAL HALF OF CAVITY   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN  MEDIAL HALF OF CAVITY   EXCISION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE REMOVED_DATE OUT OF 3  SPANNING AT LEAST 0 5CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  PRESENT ON AT LEAST 4 OUT OF 7 SLIDES  SEE NOTE  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FLORID USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  There are small foci of extruded mucin which are suspicious for the presence of invasive carcinoma  however  the possibility that these foci represent artifactual rupture of mucin into the stroma cannot be entirely excluded  In one focus  myoepithelial markers  calponin  p63  and myosin  are helpful in establishing the presence of in situ carcinoma  In another focus  however  the area of concern is not present on deeper levels  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 5 OUT OF 5 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Keratin positive tumor cells are not identified on six  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mammographic localization   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm breast excision specimen oriented with a short stitch on its superior edge  and a long stitch on its lateral edge  The long axis of the specimen is superior inferior and the specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  medial green  lateral yellow  There are two needle localization wires entering the specimen on its anterior inferior surface which mark two masses  one adjacent to the hook and