d precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 13 31     ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     THE INVASIVE TUMOR IS FOCALLY REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE SUPERIOR MARGIN AND REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE POSTERIOR MARGIN  NOTE  Although the close margin in slides E and F is not inked blue  it is at the junction of the green  anterior  and black  posterior  inks and opposite the yellow  inferior   and therefore is interpreted as superior  Added by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 12 04 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast tumor short superior  long lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 7cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with two black stitches designating the superior and lateral margins  The specimen has a localization wire in place  The posterior margin is inked black  anterior green  inferior yellow  and superior blue  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a metal clip surrounded by a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm hemorrhagic focus  The fibrous tissue shows diffuse yellow orange foci and is focally dense with no discrete lesion  Representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral as A F with the hemorrhagic focus as D F and the area designated by the clip and localization wire as F  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary lymph node stitch at highest lymph node  is a 11 x 8 x 3 0cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with a black stitch at one end designated as highest lymph node as per requisition  The specimen is divided into levels high  mid and low  Sectioning of the highest level reveals seven tan red lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 9cm in greatest dimension  Sectioning of the mid level reveals eleven tan red lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm in greatest dimension  Sectioning of the lowest level reveals a single 1 9cm tan red lymph node  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as follows  G  Highest lymph node bisected H  Five whole lymph nodes from the highest level I  One lymph nodes bisected from the highest level J  Five whole lymph nodes from the mid level K  One lymph node bisected from the mid level L  Three whole lymph nodes from mid level M  Two whole lymph nodes from mid level N  One whole lymph node bisected from the lowest level Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  inferior lateral final shaved margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with no orientation  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  the specimen is entirely submitted as O S  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  superior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm portion of unremarkable tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with no orientation  The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted as T  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  JOHN BISSONNETTE  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Sarah P Thayer  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSECTION PART B  BREAST  INFERIOR LATERAL   FINAL SHAVED MARGIN PART C  BREAST  SUPERIOR   MARGIN PART D  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
