Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  15 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  15 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 18 51 CLINICAL DATA  Cancer of left breast  status post Lump Ax                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  MASTECTOMY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU FOCALLY EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  CARCINOMA IN LYMPHATIC VESSELS  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 46                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  are two fragments of fibrofatty breast tissue  The largest of which is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm skin ellipse containing a nipple as well as a REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm skin ellipse which is 6 2cm lateral to the skin ellipse containing the nipple  The second mentioned fragment of skin also has a 5 5cm scar  In addition to the larger specimen there is also an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of breast tissue  The largest specimen is inked entirely in black and sectioned to reveal an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 6cm area of dense parenchyma underlying the nipple and extending away from the second skin ellipse and extending to the deep inked resection margin  A representative section of this area is submitted in A  No biopsy site is identified beneath the second skin ellipse which contains the scar  however a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm area of firm gritty white tan tissue is present between the two skin ellipses and above a large defect in the breast parenchyma  This firm gritty area grossly extends to the deep posterior resection margin  A representative section is submitted in B and C  Section of this firm area with deep margin in D  with anterior margin in E  Representative section of second described skin ellipse with entire thickness of underlying fat in F  Gross Description by  RHONDA YANTISS  MD Resident  ERIN OCHOA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT  MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  31 MAY 94 ACCESSIONED ON  31 MAY 94 at 14 58 CLINICAL DATA  45 year old female with left breast carcinoma by outside biopsy  with palpable lymph nodes                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  98   MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  EXTENDING TO WITHIN 4 MM OF THE DEEP RESECTION MARGIN  AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  2   PRESENT ON FOUR OF EIGHT SLIDES   SEE NOTE   NOTE  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is identified  The foci of ductal carcinoma in situ are immediately adjacent to the infiltrating tumor  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Hormone receptor stains will be performed and the results reported as an addendum  2  HEMOSIDERIN LADEN MACROPHAGES  CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  AND FIBROSIS CONSISTENT WITH BIOPSY CAVITY  SOFT TISSUE  LEFT BREAST   ADDITIONAL DEEP TISSUE MARGIN    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  SOFT TISSUE AND LYMPH NODES  AXILLA  LEFT   EXCISION  METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA IN TWO OF TWELVE LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  SOFT TISSUE   ADDITIONAL  AXILLA  LEFT   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE OF ONE LYMPH NODE EXAMINED  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 31                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   MASS    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm lumpectomy specimen with long stitch designating lateral and short stitch designating superior  The specimen contains an overlying skin ellipse that measures REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  with a 2 5cm linear  healed incision  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 2cm in greatest dimension  ill defined area of firm  tan tissue with a central gray  necrotic area  that extends to within 0 5cm of the overlying skin ellipse and 4 0cm of the deep margin  The surrounding breast parenchyma is tan white to yellow and rubbery  No other lesions are grossly identified  A frozen was done of the suspicious area and saved frozen  SECTION CODE  A  necrotic focus with deep resection margin  representative section  B  necrotic focus with inferior r