Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 02 CLINICAL DATA  2mm infiltrating ductal carcinoma with positive margin  and ductal carcinoma in  situ on biopsy at outside hospital  now undergoing a lumpectomy and axillary dissection                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL INFILTRATING OR IN SITU CARCINOMA  ENTIRELY SUBMITTED   LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY   BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 13 OF 13 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 17 07                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  and unit number  are two parts  Labeled  Left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm lumpectomy specimen with 1 5cm overlying skin ellipse  a long stitch  implies lateral and short stitch implies superior  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm biopsy cavity consisting of soft brown to tan tissue which is 1 0cm from the lateral  long stitch  resection margin and 1 0cm from the overlying skin ellipse  In the superior direction and adjacent to this is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm ill defined firm white area  2 5cm from the short stitch  1 8cm from the long stitch and 1 0cm from the overlying skin ellipse  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes A through J from the lateral stitch to the superior or short stitch  The entire biopsy cavity is submitted in B through D  with the firm area in E  Labeled  Left axillary node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm segment of red to tan fibrofatty tissue  There are multiple lymph nodes that are ta