Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  29 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  29 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 22 CLINICAL DATA  Positive FNA  A mastectomy is planned  please confirm malignancy  Status post left radical mastectomy elsewhere in  REMOVED_CASE_ID   now with a new right breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   INCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR FROZEN SECTION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3 OF 3  REMOVED_DATE CM  MEASURED FROM SLIDE   EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  SEE NOTE  NOTE  No blood vascular or lymphatic invasion is seen  An in situ component is not identified  A brisk lymphoid response is present  BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY AND AXILLARY DISSECTION  FOCUS OF LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  WITH PAGETOID SPREAD INTO A DUCT  FAT NECROSIS AND SLIGHT ACUTE AND CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH MODERATE DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA IN THE BREAST  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 10 OF 10 AXILLARY NODES   ONE NODE HAS A CAPSULAR REST OF NEVUS CELLS  SECTION N   LYMPH NODES  RIGHT SENTINEL   REGIONAL DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY 3 OF 3 NODES  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL TISSUE    REGIONAL DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 4 OF 4 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 18 13                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  are two fragments of breast  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm  The smaller is inked and sectioned to reveal a stellate  firm  white tan gritty nodule which grossly abuts the inked margin  Half is frozen as FX 1 and is saved frozen  The remainder of the tumor is submitted in cassette A  The larger fragment is inked and sectioned to reveal yellow parenchyma with no discrete lesions  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes B C  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm white skin ellipse with an unremarkable eccentric nipple areolar complex  There is a linear sutured 4 5cm incisi