ctioning reveals two poorly defined  fibrous areas identified by two localization wires and clips  The superior fibrous area measures 0 8cm in diameter and shows contraction  It is located 1 5cm from the superior  1 5cm from the medial  4 0cm from the lateral  8 0cm from the inferior  0 4cm from the superficial and 1 0cm from the deep margin  The second radial fibrous area measures 1 5cm in diameter and is located 2 0cm from the lateral end medial  1 2cm from the inferior  6 5cm from the superior  0 3cm from the superficial and 1 5cm from the deep margin  The superior mass is located 1 0cm from the deep margin  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Superior mass in relationship to the superficial and lateral margins  B  Superior nodule in relationship to the deep margin  C  Superior nodule in relationship to the superficial and lateral margins  this area has been submitted entirely in cassettes A C  D  Inferior nodule  in relationship to the deep margin  full cross section  E G  Inferior mass in relationship to the inferior margin  H  Unremarkable adipose tissue adjacent  deeply to the inferior nodule  I  Unremarkable adipose tissue adjacent laterally to the inferior nodule  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary sentinel node  are two fatty soft tissues measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm each  A lymph node is dissected from each  bisected and half of each is frozen as FX  1 2  now submitted in cassettes J K respectively  The remaining lymphoid tissue is submitted in cassette L  M and N  bivalved  and  O and ZZ separated   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margins  inferior  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x up to 1 5cm specimen which is unoriented  The specimen is serially sectioned reveal focal areas of fibrosis but no definite masses  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes P Y  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margins  medial  right breast  is a fibroadipose specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The unoriented specimen is unoriented  serially sectioned and submitted in cassettes Z GG  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margins  lateral  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x up to 1 5cm fibroadipose tissue specimen which is unoriented  The specimen is inked black  serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes HH NN  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shave margins  superior  right breast  are 3 fibroadipose tissue fragments measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes OO RR  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional axillary lymph node  right  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm adipose tissue mass containing 5 lymph nodes submitted as follows  SS  1 lymph node bivalved  TT  2 lymph nodes bivalved  UU  Adiposee tissue  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional right axillary lymph node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm lymph node with minor amount of additional adipose tissue  The lymph node is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes VV WW  Resident  MASSIMO D APUZZO  MD PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 2  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY  SENTINEL   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN TWO NODES  O R  Resident  NICOLE ANN BELSLEY  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  RE