at the periphery of the wall is firm but sharply delineated  No grossly evident invasive lesion is identified  This cavity is 3 5cm from the closest deep margin  3 0cm from the closest inferior margin  4 0cm from the closest superior margin  and 3 5cm deep to the skin ellipse  Sectioning through the remainder of the breast parenchyma reveals unremarkable fatty breast tissue with scattered areas of white  rubbery  fibrous tissue with intermixed pink tan speckles representing breast lobules  No other localized lesions are identified in the remaining breast tissue  Section Code A   Representative sections of deep margin  B G   Representative sections from around the biopsy cavity  H   Representative sections from the medial half of the breast  I   Representative sections from the central portion of the breast  J   Representative sections from the lateral portion of the breast  K   Skin incision and superior margin  L M   Nipple  N BB DD   Axillary lymph nodes  the largest of which measures 4 0cm in greatest diameter  Most of these nodes are very fatty and fleshy  Note  Cassettes U and W BB and DD each represent one lymph node each  Also received in the same specimen container is a specimen jar  labeled  lymph node   It contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm fragment of adipose tissue and intermixed lymph node  It is submitted entirely in cassette CC  Resident  C  Diana Jordan  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Wiley Souba  MD Noah Chan H Choi  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST AND LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES , Unchecked.
