nt at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 11 42 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is an oriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm yellow fibrofatty breast tissue with a wire present  Two sutures are present and are designated short stitch superior and long stitch lateral  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior  blue  deep  black  lateral  green and medial  yellow  The wire runs along the lateral aspect superior to inferior  On the anterior portion of the tissue  a suture line is present  The suture line is removed to reveal a central white tan cavity running from superior medial to the mid portion lateral  On cut section the area surrounding the cavity is white tan and extends to the black inked deep margin  No definitive mass is grossly identified  There are scattered  clear fluid filled cysts present  The specimen is entirely submitted in A L from superior to inferior  cavity in cassettes C G   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  sentinel node  hot and blue  left axilla  level 1   REMOVED_CASE_ID    REMOVED_CASE_ID   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm red brown lymph node with attached yellow tan adipose tissue  The specimen is bisected to reveal a blue cut surface  Specimen is entirely submitted in cassette M  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  final shave margin  medial half of cavity  are four unoriented fragments of fibrofatty breast tissue measuring in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  The fragments are serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes N P  Re