tained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 09 41 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm irregular firm ill defined tan yellow stellate area extending to the inked margin at one aspect of the specimen  This specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A through F  with the lesion in A through C  Resident  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST  BIOPSY  SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  BUT TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Metin Ozdemirli  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Paul Snowden Russell  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST LESION   report_end  , Unchecked.
