NG FOR HER 2 c erbB 2 Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows    Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells    Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells    Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   30  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Friday May 29   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01 31 49PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Breast  Left   Simple Mastectomy PART B  Lymph Nodes  Left Axilla Contents   Dissection PART C  Breast  Left Additional Margin Superior Aspect   Excision PART D  Breast  Right Superficial Margin Superior Flap   Excision PART E  Breast  Right Superficial Margin Inferior Flap   Excision  report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON  23 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 12 55 CLINICAL DATA  DCIS  with prior radiation for Hodgkin s                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  MULTIPLE FOCI THROUGHOUT THE LATERAL ASPECT OF THE BREAST  SEE NOTE  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  NOTE  Minimal invasion cannot be excluded  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor  Despite extensive examination  only one lymph node was detected within the axillary soft tissue  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 10 54                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast and axillary sampling   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 3cm simple mastectomy specimen  with REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm of axillary tail and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm irregular overlying skin ellipse containing an eccenterically located nipple  The specimen is oriented with the short stitch marking superior and the long stitch marking lateral  The entire specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal dense fibrous breast parenchyma which has focally diffused gritty areas  in the right upper outer and right lower quadrants  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  Many of these areas contain small firm cysts averaging in size 0 3cm  Two of thse gritty areas are frozen as FX 1  The closest of these gritty cystic lesions comes to within 0 9cm of the deep