er metal clip is noted within the specimen  No secondary clip is grossly appreciated  No other gross abnormalities are identified  Representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial end  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire gray white  stellate area  with tissue containing a silver metal clip as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral end margin  enface  Received are 3 containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin and labeled  left axillary contents   are 2 fragments of fatty tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  On dissection  several tan pink and tan gray lymph nodes are identified measuring from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  The larger lymph nodes are serially sectioned or bisected  A few lymph nodes show partial replacement by fatty tissue  All the lymph nodes are entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Largest lymph nodes  serially sectioned and entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Next 4 larger lymph nodes  each bisected and submitted entirely  1 lymph node per each cassette   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Smaller 9 candidate lymph nodes  submitted in toto  Received in formalin  and labeled  left breast final inferior margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue  A stitch represents final margin and the stitched surface is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  and labeled  left breast final superior margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x up to 1 5cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue  A stitch marks the final margin and the stitched surface is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   cassette  REMOVED_A