tibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 08 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue with a short stitch indicating the superior margin and a long stitch marking the lateral aspect of the specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned superiorly to inferiorly to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm ill defined  tan gray firm area  0 2cm from the posterior margin  1 2cm from the medial margin  and 1 0cm from the lateral margin  In addition  the lesion is 0 5cm from the inferior margin and 0 5cm from the anterior margin  as well as 0 7cm from the superior margin  Representative sections of the tumor in relation to the posterior margin are submitted in cassettes A and B  Representative sections of the lateral resection margin are submitted in C  Representative sections of the superior margin are in D  Representative sections of the inferior margin submitted in cassette E  Representative sections of the anterior margin are submitted in cassette F  Labeled  axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue from which numerous lymph nodes are dissected and submitted in cassettes G through I  Labeled  additional axillary tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue which is submitted entirely in cassette J  Labeled  additional shaved margins  are two fragments of fibroadipose tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm in size  Specimen was submitted entirely in cassettes K through M  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue containing a tan soft lymph node  1 8cm in greatest dimension  Half of the node is frozen as FX 1  now in cassette N  The remainder of the tissue is submitted entirely in cassette O  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     LYMPH NODE  AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  IVANA DELALLE  MD  PHD O R  Diagnosis by  HENRY DONG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Simon Powell  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODES  ADDITIONAL LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION PART D  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN    EXCISION PART E  LYMPH NODE  AXILLA   EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
